  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Handbook of Qualitative and Visual Methods in Spatial Research (2024), published by Transcript-Verlag, has been cited 5 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 351 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Handbook of Qualitative and Visual Methods in Spatial Research by Anna Juliane Heinrich, Séverine Marguin, Angela Million and others was published by Transcript-Verlag in 2024. It is part of the Re-Figuration von Räumen series. Conceptually, the work connects to Computer science, Cognitive science and Psychology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 5 citations. Citations peaked in 2025 with 3 citing works. Notable citing venues include Land, City and Urban Planning. The citing works include 4 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 5 countries, led by Germany, Spain and Indonesia.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 351 times via Ubiquity Press. Open Library reports a combined count of 2 reading logs and catalog editions.</p>",
